// A step that discharges a GUARDED-SORT obligation must not be reported dead under `--fast`.
//
// `permFixesPoint` binds `forall f: Perm`, and `Perm = Fn where invertible` is a REFINED sort,
// so specializing it at the plain `Fn` `g` owes `invertible(g)`. The only thing in scope that
// discharges that is `@g-invertible` — the step is LOAD-BEARING, not dead.
//
// STRICT meets the obligation while instantiating the accelerant's synthetic schema:
// `Elab.emitArgObligations` sees the refined param sort and calls `requireKnown` →
// `dischargeGoal` → `refForKnown`, which appends the supplying step to `known.reachable`, the
// use-all-facts walk's seed list. `produceSpecialize` returns at its `admit_mode` check before
// resolving the head at all, so under `--fast` none of that runs and the step looks unused.
//
// The guard is meant to be FOUND, not named: it is a side condition on a term the author
// wrote, so `requireKnown`'s search is the right mechanism. What `--fast` lacks is only the
// bookkeeping that search leaves behind — so the use-all-facts lint does not run on a proof
// containing an admitted step (it could only false-positive there), and this file is gated
// BOTH ways. Invariant: `--fast` never reports an error strict does not.
sort Element
sort Fn
pred invertible(f: Fn)
sort Perm = Fn where invertible
func apply(f: Fn, x: Element) => Element
const point: Element

// specializing this at a plain Fn incurs the guard obligation `invertible(f)`
axiom permFixesPoint: forall f: Perm; apply(f, point) = point

theorem aGuardDischargerIsNotDead: forall g: Fn; invertible(g) -> apply(g, point) = point
proof
  @generalize-g |
    fix g: Fn {
      @given-invertible |
        assume invertible(g) {
          @g-invertible |
            invertible(g)
            [by hypothesis given-invertible]
          @applied |
            apply(g, point) = point
            [using specialize permFixesPoint(g)]
        }
      @conclusion-implication |
        invertible(g) -> apply(g, point) = point
        [by discharge given-invertible]
    }
  @conclusion |
    forall g: Fn; invertible(g) -> apply(g, point) = point
    [by generalize generalize-g]
qed
